@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased (local rate-limit Groq 429 handling)
+
+On HTTP 429 the Groq provider waits using Retry-After, x-ratelimit-reset-tokens, or a "try again in Xs" message, capped at 65 seconds and at most two waits per item, then retries. Calls are paced to a 6000 input-tokens-per-minute budget (of Groq's 7000 ITPM). Wait counts are written to `export/ai-vision.json`.
+
+Tests: `tests/test_ai_vision_groq.py` (mock HTTP, no live calls).
+
 ## Unreleased (local branch feat/groq-ai-vision)
 
 A Groq provider can transcribe items still held after the enhance retry and the 400 dpi page-region retry. It is off by default. A private runner can enable it with environment variables. The default model is `qwen/qwen3.8-27b`, temperature is 0, and images are sent as data URIs with a User-Agent header. The API key is read only from `GROQ_API_KEY` and is never logged or written to reports. A per-run cap (default 50 calls), a timeout, and a small retry limit protect usage. The Qwen model accepts at most 3 images in one request, so more than 3 held crops are stitched into one image. The 400 dpi `crop-*` files are preferred. `CERTPASSLY_USE_COMMITTED_AI_READS=false` or `--ignore-committed-ai-reads` skips committed `review/ai-reads.json` so the live provider does the reads. Acceptance still uses the original dual OCR passes and the PDF text layer. Failures stay on the review sheet with the AI text as a suggestion. Provenance (model, request time, image sha256, call count) is written to `export/ai-vision.json`.
